==English==

===Etymology===
From [[Utopia]], a term coined by Sir [[w:Thomas More|Thomas More]] in his work of the same title, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|οὐ|tr=ou||not, no|sc=Grek}} + {{term|τόπος|tr=topos||place|sc=Grek}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[ideal|Ideal]] but often [[impractical]]; [[visionary]].
#: ''a '''utopian''' project''
# of or pertaining to or resembling a utopia
#: '''''utopian''' happiness''

====Synonyms====
* [[unrealistic]]

